<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-006-AL9>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-006-AL9" ;
  triage:title "AL.9 required independent review of matrix/reference-graph/cutover-table/ledger-input not obtained" ;
  triage:description "req-qa (AL9-QA-1, 2026-08-07) flags that sprint-AL9-physical-proof-ledger-freeze.md requires an independent review of the physical proof matrix, AL.8 live-reference graph capture, cutover table, and removal-ledger input, but no such independent review has been obtained/recorded yet at head 9b4c4799. Verify sprint doc's exact independent-review requirement language and confirm no record of it exists in the branch's docs. INDEPENDENT REVIEW (quality-mgr, 2026-08-10, integrate/phase-al@d8eac064): reviewed all four required artifacts. (1) AL9-live-reference-graph.md (captured at 9ceb7bee): sound -- call chains (CliComposition::send, GraftClient::send_message both via preferred_local_client->HttpRuntimeClient) match the codebase, retained-legacy-consumer table has correct AM.1 disposition rows, no internal inconsistencies found. (2) AL9-cutover-table.md: structurally complete, all 6 adapter rows document the one-listener/one-publisher invariant with retire/rollback actions; the invariant is documented but not runtime-verified, which is the separately-tracked ATM-QA-007-AL9 gap, not a defect in this table. (3) AL9-physical-proof-matrix.md: local/UDS/loopback rows cite real, checkable test names; CLI/graft write-selection rows are static/source proof only; M5 and Windows rows are stale (say 'documented rerun required'/'pending, no artifact' despite AL.13/AL.14 already producing that class of evidence elsewhere in the repo under a different doc lineage -- a doc cross-reference gap tracked as ATM-QA-002/003-AL9, not evidence of no work). No graft-specific runtime evidence found anywhere in the repo's smoke artifacts (crosshost-send/ack and Windows FastPC4 runs are CLI atm send/read/ack traffic only) -- ATM-QA-004-AL9's graft gap is real and unresolved. (4) Removal-ledger input: AM.1's sprint doc requires exactly the live-reference-graph artifact as its freeze input, and it exists in the form AM.1 specifies -- satisfied. VERDICT: the required independent review has now been performed and is recorded in this finding. It surfaces no new defects; it confirms the already-tracked gaps (002/003 doc-sync, 004/007 genuinely open, both explicitly parked pending the integration->develop review per team-lead/user directive to run no further smoke tests before then). Closing this finding on that basis." ;
